SCOPE, AND WHAT THIS LICENSE DOES NOT COVER

The MIT terms above apply to the contents of this repository: the skills, the
scripts, the taxonomy and design documents, and the brand assets.

They do NOT apply to, and this repository does not redistribute:

1. The nuclear-physics codes the per-code skills drive. Every skill obtains its
   code from that code's own upstream distribution at install time, so each
   user receives it directly from its authors under the authors' own terms.
   Those terms vary and some are not open source at all: Sky3D is distributed
   under the Computer Physics Communications non-profit use licence, and
   several others are GPL-2.0 or GPL-3.0. Read the licence of any code you
   install through a skill; a commercial user should contact that code's
   authors directly.

2. The opencode editor this platform is built on. That fork lives in a separate
   repository (github.com/jinleiphys/fusion-core) and carries its own MIT
   licence and copyright notice from the upstream project
   (github.com/anomalyco/opencode).

3. The papers summarised under kb-wiki/. Those pages contain third-party
   material: see kb-wiki/README.md for what they are, on what basis they are
   distributed, and how to ask for one to be removed. The MIT grant above does
   not purport to license anyone else's copyrighted work.
